<v Jillian Welsh>And so I was standing there, and I was getting ready to hail a cab, finishing up the end of the cigarette, and I felt him come up next to me. And yeah, he just-- it was kind of like-- I remember him just like brushing back hair kind of off of my cheek. And it's that moment, you know, where you know that you're actually going to kiss. You just feel it in your two bodies. And he just so very lightly pressed his lips up against mine. And then it was like, well, now like an actual deeper kiss. And I know from the outside, we made it look good, because it very much felt like one of those-- like a good stage kiss.
<v Jillian Welsh>所以我就站在那儿，准备拦辆出租车，抽完最后一口烟，我感觉到他走到了我身边。然后，是的，他只是……我记得他把我的头发从脸颊上拨开。那一刻，你知道，你知道你们真的要接吻了。你只是在两人的身体里感受到了。他轻轻地把嘴唇压在我的唇上。然后就像，嗯，现在变成了一个真正的深吻。我知道从外面看，我们看起来不错，因为它确实很像电影里的那种——那种高质量的舞台之吻。

